atlas forwarding

architecture address-plane
  subscribes EligibleProviders
  subscribes ReachableCapacity
  consumes Authority
  consumes ProviderState
  consumes SurfaceCandidate
  consumes FPQRepresentation
  consumes KVPassport
  consumes Capability
  publishes RouteAdvertisement
  canonical_name AddressPlane
  family forwarding
  domain Forwarding / Eligibility
  layer forwarding
  semantic_question Of all the state available, what is even eligible to participate in this operation?
  purpose A compiled bit-mask and ternary forwarding plane under the plural semantic estate. Rejects vast populations with (have & need)==need before any graph is walked, so semantic richness never becomes slow.
  maturity implemented
  node_types BitRegistry
  node_types Mask
  node_types TernaryState
  node_types Route
  edge_types eligible_for
  edge_types blackholes
  internal_calculus bitwise eligibility (have & need)==need
  internal_calculus ExternalEstate candidate forwarding: deterministic declared axis/term registry -> 62-bit-safe masks -> required intersection plus prohibited-term rejection before exact owner work
  internal_calculus temporal forwarding: ExternalEstate temporal owner classification -> bearing publication modes only -> explicit temporal AddressAxis -> shared masks; not_evident emits no negative coordinate
  internal_calculus CandidateAdvertisement compilation: canonical owner emission -> typed descriptor and declared dependency references -> shared deterministic mask registry -> kind partition -> required/prohibited cut -> exact verifier
  internal_calculus provider embedding forwarding: a complete ProviderState embedding run with every requested projection stored -> durable ProviderEmbeddingRun FactDelta -> typed latent provider CandidateAdvertisement (provider/model/representation/embedding coordinates only) -> shared mask cut -> ProviderCompiler exact run recheck and unrequested derived capability artifact -> later purpose-bound ResourceAdmission; provider vectors remain a representation, never semantic owner state
  internal_calculus physical representation export: every currently compiled CandidateAdvertisement, including all 4,891 ExternalEstate occurrences, -> content-digested declared RepresentationPassport with one shared address-index basis plus a typed binding -> PhysicalCompiler dense handles and operation support rows; runtime receipts remain separate before any cost claim
  internal_calculus durable publication/change worker: CMS, TargetObligation, ProviderState, ModelCatalog, ProtocolCommons and authenticated MCP closure snapshots preflight into a disposable generation then atomically replace only their retired owner populations; that generation emits a fsync'd content-digested physical-passport snapshot to PhysicalCompiler only through an optional native ResourceAdmission snapshot-build grant (ADMIT, DEFER, and REJECT remain separate, with a released transient grant after compilation); PhysicalCompiler atomically replaces dense handles only when the snapshot digest moved; WebAddress and ForeignTwin FactDeltas atomically enqueue each declared dependency cut with its lowerer reference, then fsync+rename one idempotent handoff envelope into that lowerer’s inbox
  internal_calculus resource-weather material reheat: the native refresh worker invokes BonfyreProject only as `foreign reheat --dry-run`, validates and atomically publishes its whole-census ResourceWeather snapshot, then advances a durable content-addressed frontier. A source's tier or scheduler decision transition produces a FactDelta named by both snapshot digests and targets only still-leased intent carrying that exact source coordinate: an initial pending lease may admit HOT/WARM material work, while a current HOT/WARM lease refreshes only on its exact `not due -> due` delta. COLD/FROZEN retain demand; WebSub -> ForeignTwin owns the later bounded read/receipt loop. Cancellation remains lease-owned and prevents a later HOT delta from resurrecting a zero-lease intent.
  internal_calculus McpApertureIR compilation: authenticated actor/address/target/policy closure digests plus typed MCP and MediaLibrary CandidateAdvertisements -> the shared required/prohibited mask cut -> deterministic content-addressed private aperture containing only resource/resource-template/tool/prompt descriptors and their exact verifier references; a valid refreshed closure atomically retires absent derived MCP descriptors without touching their owners; list eligibility remains separate from later gateway authorization
  internal_calculus ternary proof vector (+1 proven / 0 unresolved / -1 KnownNonCause)
  internal_calculus authority mask compiled from non-revoked in-window grants
  invariant a host is an institution in a territory, never a deployment; the same code and the same surfaces answer on leaflounge.aurekai.shop and theleaflounge.store, for a different subject
  invariant WebAddress binds a public subject only through an exact built-in territory apex/www address or the latest published SitePresentation for that normalized host; a suffix alone cannot bind an arbitrary subdomain, a malformed port is refused, and a truncated subject address is never accepted
  invariant the institution holding an address is published, not only stored; a surface that cannot name whose host it is standing on is a projection of nobody, and deriving it from the hostname is wrong for exactly the institution that carries a domain of its own
  invariant an institution's other territories come from the Matrix rather than from string surgery on the hostname, because the one case that matters -- an owned domain -- has no subdomain to cut up
  invariant the address document answers any origin; cross-territory resolution is the point of an address plane, and a browser refusing it is the plane failing rather than the estate protecting anything. Nothing else gains that: a gated pattern stays gated
  invariant a surface links a subject's address only where that address resolves; this estate runs 103 capabilities it does not address, and a page linking all of them would be inventing 99 addresses to look complete
  invariant bits are a compiled machine index, not meaning
  invariant the 4,891 ExternalEstate occurrences compile as external_occurrence CandidateAdvertisements from canonical occurrence terms and contain no copied body, provider state, authority, evidence or effect fact
  invariant temporal:not_evident is epistemic absence, not temporal:false, a prohibition, a static-state claim, or a candidate eligibility fact; only owner-classified bearing modes enter the temporal forwarding axis
  invariant candidate kind remains typed before selection; an ExternalEstate occurrence and a CMS-declared external source cannot become a renderer, provider, protocol enactment or compute placement because they share an eligible bit
  invariant a published World source reference compiles its exact CMS source coordinate, its publication-source coordinate and its retained ForeignTwin topic into that World advertisement's dependency set; a receipt-bound observation or a post-commit CMS publication delta therefore reaches only the declared World `SurfaceIR` cut, never a global foreign refresh
  invariant CandidateAdvertisement carries only reproducible coordinates and owner/lowerer/verifier references; it contains no copied authority, provider weather, evidence, proof, commitment or effect state
  invariant a FactDelta dependency hit produces an affected recomputation cut only; it cannot itself select, authorize, prove or execute a candidate
  invariant MaterialCompiler emits an observation request only; WebSub's durable SourceDirty ingress coalesces that request by topic and the later ForeignTwin owner independently applies observe-right, robots and receipt law before any body or FactDelta can exist
  invariant a ForeignTwin-caused MaterialCompiler handoff retains its causal write set and may materialize only the matching owner receipt reference; it cannot create another observation request for that same receipt-driven cut
  invariant a ResourceWeather FactDelta is a source-standing coordinate, not a semantic fact, source selection, authority, read grant, observed body or evidence result; it can wake only matching still-leased physical intent: an initial pending lease, or an already-admitted HOT/WARM lease whose exact scheduler decision newly became due
  invariant an MCP aperture digest is a cache key for a caller-scoped derived descriptor, never a bearer, actor fact, authorization decision, task completion, or proof frontier
  invariant a stateless MCP 2026 request binds its self-described JSON-RPC method and target to `Mcp-Method`/`Mcp-Name` before the adapter verifies the bearer and derives opaque closure coordinates; it can forward a call only when the current native aperture explicitly advertises that exact MCP tool, then only to the existing exact owner lane, so an HTTP header, static gateway catalog or cached aperture cannot become authority
  invariant a MediaLibrary MCP template/tool can appear only from a typed media_library aperture survivor; its actual catalog or representation-plan read derives the actor from the current Auth ActorClosure and rechecks MediaLibrary access, never from a caller coordinate, cached aperture or resource URI
  invariant a physical representation passport describes a reusable candidate index body rather than copying its owner facts; its compile result is an eligible body cut, never a selected physical plan
  invariant resource admission controls only the measured transient physical-passport snapshot aperture; a grant neither makes a candidate selected nor establishes durable representation capacity, authority, proof, or owner state
  invariant eligibility rejects the impossible; it never grants authority or proves anything
  invariant a blackholed hypothesis is negative forwarding state, not a permanent truth
  forbidden_inference eligible -> authorized
  forbidden_inference a host carrying an address -> that host granting anything
  forbidden_inference an anonymous resolution -> this reader's eligibility (eligibility is per caller; probing another territory from here answers for nobody in particular)
  forbidden_inference runnable -> addressable (the native capability book and the addressed subjects are two registers, and on this deployment they do not overlap)
  forbidden_inference a mask match -> a semantic match
  forbidden_inference a dependency intersection -> a state transition or global invalidation
  forbidden_inference a visible MCP operation -> authority to invoke it or permission to create an effect
  forbidden_inference a blackholed hypothesis -> permanently false (a reheat reopens it)
  native_format graf
