  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/clone-surfaces.test.mjs holds the published plane against the live estate: a host names the institution that holds it, an institution is one subject across its territories with one host each, an institution that carries its own domain is still found through the Matrix, the address document answers a foreign origin, and a clone links a subject's address only where that address resolves
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh imports ExternalEstate plus CMS/SiteProgram, TargetObligation, Provider, Model/compute, authenticated MCP 2026-07-28 JSON-RPC closure refresh and ProtocolCommons owner emissions; it proves a complete source generation is preflighted before atomic replacement, stale selected owner advertisements retire without touching other populations, a CMS World carries both its exact declared ForeignTwin topic and publication-source coordinate to a `SurfaceIR:world` handoff, malformed MCP output cannot replace a valid closure, a closure-scoped McpApertureIR uses the shared mask cut and carries no authority result, the worker flushes completed owner-generation receipts before forking its fsync'd RepresentationPassport snapshot so a receipt can never be misparsed as a physical declaration, invokes PhysicalCompiler only after a native ADMIT build grant and releases that transient grant, a REJECT leaves no replacement physical registry, and WebAddress-shaped CMS deltas enter only their declared lowerer queue
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh proves the retained 4,891-row corpus persists 1,156 temporal-bearing and 3,735 temporal:not_evident owner states, emits temporal terms only for bearing modes, and changes AddressPlane membership between temporal:feed and temporal:forecast while retaining eligible_for_further_consideration until ForeignTwin's exact owner check
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh proves the CMS lowering preserves what a published row declares rather than flattening it to an identity and a label: a SourceCollection carries its declared domains, source refs, material kinds and refresh policy; a CapabilityProgram carries consumes, produces, carrier candidates, capability requirements, authority requirement and transition conditions; a SiteProgram carries the experiences, bindings, collections and capability programs it composes, plus the dependency edges on each; and the forwarding cut answers a carrier, authority, flow and composition question from those terms, selects nothing for a carrier no row declared, and retires the SiteProgram composition behind its capability program's own frontier
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh holds the forwarding vocabulary to one declaration: the whole emitted population -- every CMS, TargetObligation, Provider, Model, MCP, ProtocolCommons and InformationPolicy advertisement of a real generation, not a hand-written sample beside them -- is validated against schemas/control/address-advertisement.cue, an undeclared axis is refused where a term is parsed, and the binary's own kind and axis lists are compared with the CUE declaration so the two copies cannot drift apart while both keep passing
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh proves a complete ProviderState embedding run with matching requested/stored projection counts emits a separate typed provider candidate carrying only provider/model/representation/embedding coordinates and `ProviderState:embedding_run` / `ProviderCompiler:embedding` references; it remains distinct from a generic physical provider materialization
  witness cmd/BonfyreLoweringWorkers/tests/lowering_workers_test.sh proves ProviderCompiler reopens only a complete matching ProviderEmbeddingRun and stores its provider/model/representation/dimensions as an `unrequested` derived artifact rather than admitting a later operation
  witness estate/generated/provider-embedding-delta-reconciliation-2026-09.json records two real ProviderState completion writes entering FactDelta forwarding; each cut one provider candidate and dispatched exactly one typed ProviderCompiler handoff without provider execution, semantic selection or effect
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/mcp_2026_aperture_test.sh proves the additive stateless MCP 2026 ingress rejects missing/mismatched self-description headers, verifies native bearer admission before compiling an opaque-address native aperture, exposes that closure only as a derived resource/read-only refresh result, hides the staged gateway's unadvertised static tool, refuses a call to it before forwarding, and forwards an explicitly advertised owner tool only through the exact authenticated owner lane
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/media_actor_closure_test.sh proves real native MediaLibrary and CreatorChannel advertisements become MCP resource templates/tools, an Auth-bound actor reads its own audio catalog, direct representation plan and current channel surface through the stateless MCP carrier, and revoking the same principal-to-actor binding refuses a further catalog before it reaches either owner
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/fact_delta_test.sh proves only a committed published CMS row emits an atomic FactDelta; its schema-declared unique owner coordinate and a PublicationOccurrence's exact source coordinates survive, draft rows emit no projection cut, and a configured handoff failure is explicit rather than reported as delivered
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh exports the actual mixed ExternalEstate and owner CandidateAdvertisement population as CUE-validated content-digested physical passports, compiles them into dense handles, and proves an MCP projection is only eligible for further physical consideration rather than selected
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebSub/tests/websub_test.sh proves a successful receipt-bound ForeignTwin re-observation first becomes a durable ForeignTwin FactDelta and no duplicate source reread is needed to retry its local forwarding handoff
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebSub/tests/websub_test.sh proves fifty typed MaterialCompiler observation demands coalesce through the native WebSub-owned SourceDirty ingress before one bounded ForeignTwin observation; demand acceptance emits no body, receipt, FactDelta, evidence, authority or effect
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebSub/tests/material_demand_bridge_test.sh proves a MaterialCompiler request passes through WebSub SourceDirty and a receipt-validated ForeignTwin observation, whose FactDelta reaches AddressPlane and returns as a receipt-bound material artifact without re-enqueueing the source
  witness cmd/BonfyreMaterialWeatherReheat/tests/weather_material_bridge_test.sh proves a FROZEN -> HOT ResourceWeather FactDelta admits only its held leased source, then crosses the native MaterialCompiler, WebSub SourceDirty, receipt-bound ForeignTwin and AddressPlane return path without a self-exciting reread
  witness cmd/BonfyreResourceWeatherTransition/tests/resource_weather_transition_test.sh proves an initial whole-census snapshot establishes a frontier without work, a later content-different HOT snapshot processes one source-scoped reheat delta, and retrying its exact digest produces no further material handoff
  witness cmd/BonfyreResourceWeatherTransition/tests/project_weather_transition_test.sh proves the actual BonfyreProject `foreign reheat --dry-run` schema feeds the durable transition without a foreign receipt/body
  witness cmd/BonfyreResourceWeatherRefresh/tests/resource_weather_refresh_test.sh proves the native worker atomically compiles a fixture whole-census Project weather frontier and emits one source-scoped material handoff while making no foreign read
  witness cmd/BonfyreLoweringWorkers/results/2026-09-12-external-estate-material-demand.json proves the real 4,891-source ExternalEstate population compiles one typed external-occurrence handoff through MaterialCompiler:external into exactly one rechecked ForeignTwin observation demand without reading the source
