architecture route-ranker
  canonical_name RouteRanker
  family forwarding
  domain Forwarding / Learned Optimization
  layer forwarding
  semantic_question Of the eligible survivors, which few are most likely to succeed?
  purpose A tiny ternary model (weights in {-1,0,+1}, a BitNet-shaped linear head) that ranks the funnel's survivors by predicted success, trained on the routing outcomes the system already produces. It sits after deterministic pruning; it reorders eligibles and overrides nothing.
  maturity implemented
  node_types TernaryRanker
  node_types RouteRecord
  edge_types ranks
  internal_calculus ternary linear score; weights = correlation sign thresholded to {-1,0,+1}
  invariant the ranker only reorders eligible survivors; it never changes eligibility, grants authority, or proves anything
  invariant a feature's weak signal collapses to 0 rather than pretending to matter
  cannot_infer surviving the mask -> being lawful, available, affordable or true; the cut removes what is impossible and every exact owner still decides afterwards
  cannot_infer a term on a candidate -> a grant, a proof, a provider admission, a relation, a payment or an effect right; an axis says which question a value answers, never that the answer is permitted
  cannot_infer a learned re-ordering -> a change in eligibility; the ternary head reorders survivors and can never add one, remove one, or override a gate
  cannot_infer a candidate advertisement -> the owner record it was derived from; it is disposable, it can be stale, and it replaces no owner state and no effect-time check
  cannot_infer an empty result -> the subject not existing; a cut that selects nothing is a cut, not a denial and not an absence
  forbidden_inference a high rank -> a correct or authorized route (the exact closure still verifies the top choice)
  forbidden_inference a learned weight -> a large training set (currently ~10 real workload_proven successes)
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/route_ranker.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_route_ranker.py.archive
  interacts address-plane
  source_lineage AddressPlane / BitNet learned-forwarding vision
  known_gap richer structural features (SID / masks / cost buckets / prior similar-route outcomes) and more routing-outcome records; a real BitNet backend when one exists in Bonfyre
  known_gap the canonical address resolves a shell and nothing more; the lenses that fill a subject out -- its world, its discussion, its map, its offers -- are separate reads and nothing yet hydrates them into the page
  known_gap subject addressing covers parcel, capability and note; the capability register that resolves is the priced catalogue, so 103 runnable capabilities have no address
  known_gap every source this entry names is archived, so nothing here is a live implementation a reader can open and run. Whether a native owner has taken this work over is not established in this entry; until one is named and witnessed here, the architecture stands on retired code.
